replace(d5,'''### D5 — Approved generative-AI factual authority and expressive interaction

**Issue:** R §§12–18 supersedes the restricted-clause-only proposal, backend-selected interview answer intents and universal template fallback. The approved design uses richer expression and AI-native free-text interpretation.

**Why it matters:** Factual authority and fictional opinion/expression are different. Fans can express jokes, support, anger or speculation; their text cannot create an injury, contract, trade, relationship, result, award or past quote.

**Recommended choice:** **Approved by the owner:** Game Core supplies confirmed facts/allowed context; Gemini provides rich expression and finite structured interview meaning; Application validates that interpretation; Game Core alone computes and commits consequences. Narrative prose never creates authoritative events. Raw player answers and accepted meanings are preserved; unsupported tags/references/quotes are rejected, with pending/retry states and no partial mutation. AI-native interviews/fan/SNS content need no template equivalents. The full boundary is §4.5/C43.

**Alternative:** The former engine-clause-only/universal-fallback design is superseded, not an equally approved option. Any later product restriction or broader semantic command language requires a new explicit owner change; do not silently narrow expressive content to clause rearrangement.

**Impact:** Phase 21 owns interview triggers/context/consequence rules; Phase 26 owns free-text interpretation, validation, atomic core bridge and expressive bundles. Gates prove factual-reference protection, no arbitrary mutations, idempotency, raw-answer retention and stale-request rejection. Semantic prose checking still has practical limits: no prompt/schema alone is proof of truth; reject/withhold unsupported content and test adversarial cases. This decision does not authorize production implementation.

''')
